
Welcome to Crab — serverless Git for large files.

  Get to your first push:
    1. Create a cloud bucket/container and sign in to its provider
    2. crab configure <provider://bucket/repository>
    3. crab ship . -m 'Initial commit'

  Joining an existing repository?  crab clone <remote>
  Setup not working?              crab doctor

  Guide: https://crab.build/docs/cli/getting-started/first-repository

Remote 'origin' → crab://crab/mount-large/mapped-fuse-34317ee5f64c46ffad2f89d7246c071a
OK: Credentials: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=****
Remote repository ready → crab://crab/mount-large/mapped-fuse-34317ee5f64c46ffad2f89d7246c071a

Next:
  1. crab setup            # detect large files and write .gitattributes
  2. git status            # review crab.toml and tracking rules
  3. crab ship -m 'init'   # commit and push to Crab
